Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hp.Ma.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">292c</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οὐκέτι πόρρω διθυράμβων φθέγγομαι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Phdr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">238d</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> a name of Dionysus, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">E.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ba.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">526</span> </span> (lyr.), <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Philod.Scarph.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1</span> </span>:—hence <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">Διθυραμβογενής</span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">AP</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.524</span> </span>. (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> </span> is said to have written it <span class=\"gk\">λυθίραμβος</span> (<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">85</span> </span>)—as if from <span class=\"gk\">λῦθι ῥάμμα,</span> the cry of Bacchus when sewn up in his father's thigh.)</div></div>"}